[ti:Day 14]

[00:00.00]vita [ˈviːtə]n. 个人简历
[00:02.16]hierarchy [ˈhaɪərɑːki]n. 等级制度；统治集团；领导层 例 The lady in red clothes is high up in the management hierarchy. 搭 a sense of hierarchy 等级观念
[00:15.48]secretarial [ˌsekrəˈteəriəl]a. 秘书的；书记的；部长的 例 She could not afford to pay off the mortgage payment after losing her secretarial job.
[00:29.04]lading [ˈleɪdɪŋ]n. 装船；装载
[00:31.68]isolated [ˈaɪsəleɪtɪd]a. 孤立的；单独的；分离的 例 It is not an isolated business case.
[00:39.48]vendor [ˈvendə(r)]n. 卖主，卖方；小贩
[00:42.72]innovate [ˈɪnəveɪt]vi. 创新，改革 vt. 创立，创始 例 It's hard for us to innovate if there's a great difficulty in attracting investors. Italy's smaller banks will also come under scrutiny. 搭 innovate in/upon/on 在…方面进行创新
[01:03.96]audience [ˈɔːdiəns]n. 观众；听众；读者；受众；拥护者； 陈述意见的机会；正式接见 例 If your audiences don't have an obvious reason to be interested, tell them why they should listen to you. 搭 give audience to 听，倾听 / have an audience with 拜会
[01:25.08]inscrutable [ɪnˈskruːtəbl]a. 不能预测的；难以理解的；不可 思议的 例 It's one of the world's leading and somewhat inscrutable technology companies.
[01:38.64]merchandise [ˈmɜːtʃəndaɪs]n. [总称]商品；货物 [ˈmɜːtʃəndaɪz]vt. 经商；推销 例 Under what circumstances can the distributor return merchandise to the manufacturer?
[01:54.60]quagmire [ˈkwæɡmaɪə(r)]n. 沼泽地；难以解脱的困境
[01:58.80]frequency [ˈfriːkwənsi]n. 频率；发生次数 例 If you want to save money and increase your productivity, you do well to reduce the number and frequency of such stupid decisions.
[02:15.60]utensil [juːˈtensl]n. 器具 搭 cooking utensil 烹饪器具 / household utensil 家用器皿
[02:23.04]disposal [dɪˈspəʊzl]n. 清除；处置；支配；解决 搭 at one's disposal 由某人支配 / waste disposal 废物处理
[02:31.56]apparent [əˈpærənt]a. 明显的，显而易见的；表面上的， 貌似(真实)的 例 In that case, the benchmark should be adjusted so that any further slowdown will become apparent the next time.
[02:47.88]afloat [əˈfləʊt]a./ad. 浮在水面(的)；在船上(的)；(经济 上)应付自如地(的)；在进行中(的)；(消息等)在流 传中(的) 例 During the financial crisis, he had to sell his house to keep the business afloat.
[03:04.56]precious [ˈpreʃəs]a. 珍贵的，宝贵的；贵重的 ad. 〈口〉 很，非常 搭 know precious little about sth. 对某事了解极 少
[03:13.56]embark [ɪmˈbɑːk]vt. 使从事；投(资)于；使上船(或飞 机、汽车等) vi. 从事，着手 例 More and more people are embarking money to real estate to make a fortune. 搭 embark for 乘船(或飞机、汽车等)赴… / embark on/upon 着手，从事
[03:31.80]malfunction [ˌmælˈfʌŋkʃn]n. 故障；失灵；功能失调 vi. 发生 故障；机能失常
[03:37.56]undefined [ˌʌndɪˈfaɪnd]a. 不确定的；不明确的；未下定义的
[03:42.24]proof [pruːf]n. 证据；检验；校样；样张 a. 检验用 的；防…的，耐…的 vt. 检验；校对 搭 put sth. to the proof 检验某物
[03:50.52]abdicate [ˈæbdɪkeɪt]v. 辞(职)，退(位)；正式放弃(权利、 责任等) 例 The people in Ireland, their children and even their grandchildren would have to pay off heavy debts if the government abdicated its responsibility to regulate and restrain the financial sector. 搭 abdicate sb's responsibility 不履行职责
[04:19.44]circulation [ˌsɜːkjəˈleɪʃn]n. (货币等的)流通，周转；循环； 传播；发行；发行量 搭 be taken out of circulation 退出流通领域 / in circulation 在流通的
[04:31.44]plague [pleɪɡ]n. 瘟疫；麻烦 vt. 折磨；使苦恼；使受灾 祸 例 Worries about joblessness plague most of the workforce.
[04:41.40]summon [ˈsʌmən]vt. 传唤，召唤；鼓起(勇气)；传讯(出 庭) 搭 summon the defendant 传被告
[04:48.36]backfire [ˌbækˈfaɪə(r)]vi. 产生出乎意料及事与愿违的结果 例 If history could live over, the President's proposal would backfire.
[05:00.24]talent [ˈtælənt]n. 天资，才能；人才 搭 talent for... …的才能
[05:05.28]consular [ˈkɒnslə(r)]a. 领事的；执政的 例 Both sides exchanged views on bilateral consular cooperation and other issues of common concern.
[05:18.84]mould [məʊld]n. 模型，模具；性格，气质 vt. 用模子 做；浇铸；塑造 例 The mould factory plans to expand the scale and product lines. 搭 mould...into 把…塑造成…
[05:32.04]succession [səkˈseʃn]n. 连任；继任；继承 搭 in succession to 继任的
[05:37.80]debasement [dɪˈbeɪsment]n. (品质)降低；贬值 例 Quantitative easing is supposed to be part of a general tendency towards the debasement of currencies.
[05:52.44]ignite [ɪɡˈnaɪt]vt. 点火，引燃；使激动 例 It can ignite your fighting will.
[05:59.16]tramp [træmp]n. 不定期货船
[06:01.44]auxiliary [ɔːɡˈzɪliəri]a. 辅助的；附属的；备用的，后备的 n. 辅助者；辅助物 例 Auxiliary storage devices will augment the memory capacity.
[06:13.56]recede [rɪˈsiːd]vi. 撤回，收回；跌落；降低 例 The price of my company's shares has receded now.
[06:22.08]strategy [ˈstrætədʒi]n. 战略，策略
[06:25.32]disburse [dɪsˈbɜːs]v. 支付，支出
[06:28.32]indemnity [ɪnˈdemnəti]n. 补偿；赔偿 例 The indemnity contract requires both sides to exercise the utmost faith.
[06:39.24]plaintiff [ˈpleɪntɪf]n. 起诉人，原告 搭 plaintiff sues in person 原告自诉
[06:45.72]telegraphic [ˌtelɪˈɡræfɪk]a. 电报机的，电报的；电信的
[06:50.40]duplicate [ˈdjuːplɪkeɪt]n. 完全一样的东西；复制品；副本 a. 复制的 vt. 复制，复印；重复 搭 document in duplicate 一式两份的文件
[07:00.24]adjourn [əˈdʒɜːn]vt. 使延期；使中止；休会 vi. 休会；转 移会址 例 The summit on financial crisis was adjourned for four days. 搭 adjourn to somewhere 转移至某地
[07:13.92]oversubscribe [ˌəʊvəsəbˈskraɪb]vt. 超额认购 例 The stock has been oversubscribed after its launch, so there has to be a ballot for the shares.
[07:27.84]restock [ˌriːˈstɒk]vt. 重新进货；再贮存
[07:31.32]undervalue [ˌʌndəˈvæljuː]vt. 对…评价过低；低估 例 Never undervalue women's contribution to economic development.
[07:42.48]dilemma [dɪˈlemə]n. 左右为难的状况；困境 搭 be caught in dilemma 陷入进退两难的境地 / prisoner's dilemma 囚徒困境
[07:51.72]due [djuː]a. 应付的，到期的 例 When does the bill fall due?
[07:56.76]downturn [ˈdaʊntɜːn]n. 下降趋势(尤指商业或经济活动) 例 The worst downturn since the Great Depression is only part of the problem.
[08:08.64]foreman [ˈfɔːmən]n. 领班；工头；陪审团团长 例 The boss called the foreman on the carpet for granting sick leave to a worker without first asking for permission.
[08:23.64]tag [tæɡ]n. 标签；附属物 vt. 加标签于 vi. 紧随 例 Please tag every item in the store.
[08:30.60]damages [ˈdæmɪdʒɪs]n. 损害赔偿金 例 Tom is gathering evidence to claim for damages against the entities responsible for the injuries.
[08:43.68]beware [bɪˈweə(r)]v. 小心，谨防 例 The fire department urges the public to beware of winter blazes.
[08:53.16]upkeep [ˈʌpkiːp]n. 维持；保养；保养费
[08:56.28]collapse [kəˈlæps]n./v. (使)破产；(使)崩溃；(使)暴跌； (使)倒塌；折叠 例 The economy of this nation was brought into a state of disaster, and for a time even on the brink of collapse.
[09:12.84]close [kləuz]v. 关闭；堵塞；结束；结账；缔结 n. 结 束；收盘，结转
[09:17.40]epidemic [ˌepɪˈdemɪk]n. 流行病；流传，盛行 a. 流传极广 的；传染性的 例 An unemployment epidemic is a result of economic crisis. 搭 epidemic flu 流行性感冒
[09:30.48]applicable [əˈplɪkəbl]a. (规则)可应用的；合适的；有利的 例 This section of the law is applicable only to corporations.
[09:41.28]average [ˈævərɪdʒ]a. 平均的；平常的，普通的 n. 平均 数，平均 v. 平均 例 In this simple case, customers are only described by age and average balance. 搭 on average 平均
[09:55.68]workplace [ˈwɜːkpleɪs]n. 工作场所；车间
[09:59.28]avow [əˈvaʊ]vt. 公开宣称；坦率承认；断言，坚称 例 The senator was forced to avow openly that he had received some money from that company. 搭 avow one's guilt 认罪
[10:13.68]encroachment [ɪnˈkrəʊtʃmənt]n. 侵占，侵犯；侵蚀 例 That's a sign of the encroachment of commercialism in education.
[10:24.84]slump [slʌmp]n. (物价)暴跌；萧条 vi. 大幅度下降，暴 跌；突然倒下 例 The authorities attributed the slump in retail business to increasing costs and the impact from online sales.
[10:40.80]axe [æks]n. 斧头；(经费)大削减；裁员 vt. 用斧头 削；大削减；裁员 例 The British government will cut investment spending and pensions and axe 10,000 publicsector jobs in a drive to meet EU deficit targets. 搭 give sb. the axe 解雇某人 / hang up one's axe 放弃无益的计划；洗手不干
[11:04.56]teeming [ˈtiːmɪŋ]a. 多产的；丰富的；拥挤的；热闹的
[11:08.52]steep [stiːp]a. 陡的；急剧升降的；(要求或价格)过分 的，过高的
[11:12.96]corporate [ˈkɔːpərət]a. 法人团体的，企业的，公司的；全 体的，共同的 例 In Japan and Britain, corporate investment fell by about a quarter from peak to trough. 搭 do sth. for corporate good 为共同利益做某 事
[11:30.72]pursue [pəˈsjuː]vt. (继续)实施；从事，忙于；追逐，追 赶；追求 搭 pursue a lofty goal 追求崇高的目标
[11:38.28]stockbroker [ˈstɒkbrəʊkə(r)]n. 股票经纪人，股东
[11:42.72]audit [ˈɔːdɪt]vt. 审计，检查(账目) n. 审计
[11:46.20]feasible [ˈfiːzəbl]a. 可做的；切实可行的；行得通的 例 To broaden the market in Europe seems feasible in theory but not in practice.
[11:58.08]autarky [ˈɔːtɑːki]n. 闭关自守；(经济的)自给自足 例 Figures on the decline in world trade are horrible for anybody except anti-globalisation advocates of autarky.
[12:13.56]surtax [ˈsɜːtæks]n. 附加税
[12:16.08]oversight [ˈəʊvəsaɪt]n. 监督，监管；疏忽；失察 例 To facilitate the oversight process, the government requires related divisions to report back periodically on their activities. 搭 under the oversight of 受到…的监管
[12:36.60]spur [spɜː(r)]n. 刺激(物)；激励 vt. 激励，鞭策；促进 vi. 策马飞奔 搭 on the spur of the moment 一时冲动之下， 未经仔细考虑地 / put spurs to 对…加以促进
[12:47.76]tramway [ˈtræmweɪ]n. 电车轨道
[12:50.52]accomplish [əˈkʌmplɪʃ]vt. 达到(目的)；完成(任务)；实现(计 划、诺言等) 例 The engineers have accomplished the first part of the project. 搭 accomplish one's object 达到目标 / accomplish the task 完成任务
[13:08.52]establish [ɪˈstæblɪʃ]vt. 建立，成立；确立；确定 例 We have established a long-term relationship of cooperation after many years of effort. ) / establishment n.
[13:23.76]loophole [ˈluːphəʊl]n. 观察孔；漏洞；逃避的手段 例 He employed a lawyer to find loopholes in the purchase contract.
